{"id": "EUVD-2026-103961", "enisaUuid": "8b11acc5-69ae-385a-8909-0162390774e4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: shut down RX BA session timer on teardown\n\nTearing down an RX BA session can leave the session timer queued on a\nfreed tid_rx. Later timer-wheel processing and the timer callback itself\nthen run against freed memory.\n\nAn RX BAR handler can dereference tid_rx under RCU before teardown\nunpublishes it and stay in its read-side critical section while teardown\ndeletes the session timer. The stale handler can then rearm the timer\nafter timer_delete_sync() returns and before the RCU callback frees\ntid_rx.\n\nUse timer_shutdown_sync() so rearm attempts become ineffective once\nteardown starts. Keep reorder_timer unchanged: teardown marks the session\nremoved under reorder_lock and its release path checks that state before\nrearming. session_timer has no equivalent guard because\nieee80211_rx_h_ctrl() rearms it before taking reorder_lock.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0da6ab1fc53a68025929baf0947519c6c1684dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bb2a5bd4f07192fca35644fab7d49a17bfbc861", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/481f9230284c27052b59c587069f232c5d84779e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09b7d5e4f88504e62ddf4ff31ebeebb3b87578ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e588e83e5c7a0f6d7a77dbbb58927c8c8cfd598e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8mvq-3rmc-c8vm", "CVE-2026-98707"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c0d48a6-bea9-377d-a326-de4dedc88404", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "16b5e060-6888-38dc-942a-c384c5dc5c8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a87f736d942c86255e3088c606f0e3eab6bbf784 <09b7d5e4f88504e62ddf4ff31ebeebb3b87578ba"}, {"id": "547afd57-645e-35cf-b162-c9bb837acf7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a87f736d942c86255e3088c606f0e3eab6bbf784 <e588e83e5c7a0f6d7a77dbbb58927c8c8cfd598e"}, {"id": "55a19ec2-5307-364e-8028-7051c17a2d35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a87f736d942c86255e3088c606f0e3eab6bbf784 <d0da6ab1fc53a68025929baf0947519c6c1684dc"}, {"id": "55fc6587-b851-3220-bd7f-721576eac780", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "68ca91d4-b083-37b7-b74a-7a44f57dab04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "74b7ab11-3def-39af-9149-da2916bea75e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "ad225897-25e1-3018-8f81-491176727905", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a87f736d942c86255e3088c606f0e3eab6bbf784 <7bb2a5bd4f07192fca35644fab7d49a17bfbc861"}, {"id": "bc8ac86e-29dc-3dd6-af0c-bb32311fb693", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a87f736d942c86255e3088c606f0e3eab6bbf784 <481f9230284c27052b59c587069f232c5d84779e"}, {"id": "c2fc872f-02f8-3a32-8462-c35f718cc677", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "c85f5c95-8dd0-3b4e-a815-93d1b20984b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.36"}, {"id": "dab18808-65f8-3c78-a19e-0e2d7accd3ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "798d4f11-bea0-315b-bbf0-40749fea39a4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}